WEBVTT

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.810
That was of waste of
damn time, I tell ya!

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.090
I gotta hurry back and make some money!

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.040
Huh? Where's Mr. Jikukawa?

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.270
He said he had something to do,

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.910
so we should go back to Japan without him.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.800
I'm... not goin' back.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.010
Not till I know why Rook changed.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.140
Then yer ass can stay here alone.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.760
No one's leadin' me around
by the nose anymore.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.180
I, Ana, think...

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.730
Taking a step back lets
you see the whole picture.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.020
Ana's exactly right.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:53.050
There might be things you'll see
if you take a step away.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.530
You're sure to meet again.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.530
You and Rook are connected
by puzzles, right?

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.600
Sure enough, we are
connected by puzzles...

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.510
Kaito and I.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.010
Nothing else is necessary.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.680
You called for me, Master Rook?

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:23.640
I authorize use of the
Labyrinth of Condemnation.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.300
That forbidden puzzle?

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.370
Understood.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.880
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.680
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.470
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.220
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.730
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:12.440
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.650
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.320
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:19.320
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.620
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.580
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.370
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:30.920
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.170
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:37.840
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.090
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.430
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.060
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:50.940
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.610
Brain diver

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.410
Brain diver

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.000
Labyrinth of Condemnation

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:18.380
Wow! The sky is so blue!

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.180
This Venetian scenery is like a dream.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.510
Like a dream!

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.200
Ah, you want some?

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.710
They're Nonoha sweets.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:28.300
I don't need 'em!

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.940
Why did you two even come along?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.480
We thought that, with you around,

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.980
we'd be safe even wandering
around a foreign country.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.600
Also, Italy has...

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.990
lots of great food, right?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:44.930
I thought that if they ate some,
Kaito and Cube would cheer up.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.410
Sheeit!

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:50.440
I, Ana, think Italy isn't just beautiful:

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:53.710
this is where Leo-Leo was born!

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.290
Da Vinci? Oh, that's right!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.590
And Micheli, and Gali-Gali!

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.320
Michelangelo and Galileo too, huh?

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.050
It has great food and
is awesome too, huh?

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.180
Come to think of it,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.060
Gammon, why is your title "Galileo"?

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.980
Who cares about that kinda stuff?!

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.190
Damn, why'd it have to be like this?

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.190
I can't help it, can I?

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.520
After all...

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:24.880
I won't forget you, Okabe.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:26.780
Everyone!

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.530
Please wait!

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.360
Mr. Jikukawa?

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.410
You can't get on that plane.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:40.590
It looks like the POG controls
the direct flights to Japan!

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.090
Planes above the clouds,
all rigged with traps...

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.240
It's a deadly puzzle with no escape!

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:48.090
What?!

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:49.810
How'd you manage to find that out?

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.430
I have my own information network.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.690
I had the Gakuen president
change your return route.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.730
Here are your new tickets.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:03.110
Please get some sightseeing in,
stretch your legs a little.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:06.680
So, Venice, huh?

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:11.080
Gammon and the others sure are
good with boats, huh?

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.160
I get seasick in no time.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:14.870
Say, Kaito?

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.310
Damn, this'll mess up my schedule.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.060
Ah, food!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.260
Whoa! It looks delicious!

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.190
I'm hungry!

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.740
Speakin' of, I'm gettin' hungry too.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.730
You two go buy us some food.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.580
Sure thing, leave it to us!

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.280
I'm totally countin' on ya.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.930
Let's go, Ana.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:50.780
Okay!

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:54.450
Thanks, guys!

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.660
We'll get pizza and paninis!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.500
Sorry for the wait!

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:07.220
Huh? Gammon?

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.470
Wasn't this the place?

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.380
You wanna get this thing started?

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:22.400
Oh, dear, so you noticed?

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:25.700
First the plane tickets,
then arrangin' this gondola.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:28.030
It was friggin' obvious.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.660
Well...

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.660
For starters...

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:36.540
That guy only drinks apple juice.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.580
Excellently done!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.290
You're quite good.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.420
You saw through my disguises.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:46.880
Still, this is a problem.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.560
I was ordered to guide Galileo, Da Vinci

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.360
and Edison to the puzzle, you see.

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.390
You don't need those guys.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:57.560
I can solve your weak-ass puzzles alone.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.800
My, you are interesting.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:14.120
Welcome to the POG...

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.690
Newton.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:19.370
Or should I say, Minotaur the Giver?

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.770
You can just call me "Souji."

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:22.960
Have a seat.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.470
I'm grateful for you
making this time for me,

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:31.480
Director Crossfield.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.740
Thank Baron Kaidou.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:34.970
It was his request.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.260
There's something you want to ask me?

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:42.140
Yes, a few things about
the Phi-Brain Project.

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:48.500
Ah, I would ask you not inquire

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.820
how I know such top-secret information.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.690
You should know, shouldn't you?

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:56.510
There's nothing I can say
about top-secret matters.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:58.580
<i>Master Rook...</i>

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.750
<i>Galileo has arrived.</i>

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:04.670
Gammon!

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.380
Yeah, sorry.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.340
The plan didn't work.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.730
It seems he was the superior player.

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:14.930
It's your dumb ass, huh?

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:17.840
Welcome, Gammon Sakanoue.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:24.530
This is a Puzzle of Fools from which
no one has emerged alive.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.470
It is the Labyrinth of Condemnation.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.420
Sheeit...

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:32.150
I can solve any puzzle,
no matter what kind it is!

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.170
Unfortunately, I'm sure
it's impossible for you.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:36.510
Huh?!

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:38.240
If it can be solved,

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:41.600
the only candidate is the
Armlet of Orpheus's holder, Kaito Daimon.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:42.500
Him alone.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:44.610
That fool again?

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.500
Ironic, isn't it?

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.840
Though your title is "Galileo,"

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.700
you shall lose your life here,

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:52.460
in a land closely tied to your namesake.

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:54.820
Let's get started already!

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:58.640
All this talkin' smack
ain't gonna earn me a single dime!

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:01.630
Understood.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:07.600
Gammon...

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.930
He should have been on
the direct flight back to Japan.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:18.590
You have nothing to say, do you?

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:22.830
Well, let's not exchange unpleasantries.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.120
Shall we do this instead, Director?

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.880
If I win at chess,

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.600
you will answer just one
of my questions, let's say.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:34.510
And what will you wager?

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.010
Well...

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.760
My most treasured possession.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.270
Very well.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:53.530
Five floodgates...

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:57.780
If you can clear them all,
the puzzle shall be released.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.630
The gondola can only move forward.

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:03.780
It can only be turned in
areas where the canals curve.

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:06.790
Turning at a right angle
will not be possible.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.290
These canals are pretty narrow, huh?

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.050
Each time you clear a floodgate,

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:16.390
area map data and time until
the next floodgate closes

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:18.290
will be sent to you.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.680
You must pass floodgates 1 through 5,

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.680
and all in order.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:28.110
When the countdown reaches zero,
the floodgates will close.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:32.320
At that time, the gondola's
auxiliary motor will activate.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.560
It will accelerate toward
the floodgate, and...

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:39.360
When death greets you, you will know:

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:42.100
you were nothing more than a lowly star

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:45.020
being pulled along by the sun.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:48.040
In that case, lemme tell you...

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:53.170
Both the sun and the
moon revolve around me!

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:58.170
Well then, feel free to begin.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:02.140
Do you know the rules?

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:05.840
White plays first, so
is often given to one's

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:08.220
junior or someone of lesser ability.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.060
Isn't that right?

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:13.230
I am, after all, the older of us two.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:15.390
I see.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:17.070
In that case...

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:30.390
Jeez! Where's our hotel?

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:34.070
This is all because
Gammon went and left us!

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:36.050
Ah! Gali-Gali!

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.220
If I go straight ahead,

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.700
the second floodgate will
be in front of me...

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:50.560
I ain't fallin' for an
easy trick like that.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.930
This is the right route!

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:01.260
I still can't see it...

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.950
Oh! Over there!

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.330
Gammon!

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:10.830
Stay back! This is a Puzzle of Fools!

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:15.570
Oh, no!

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:31.700
Kaito!

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:34.610
Gammon's in a Puzzle of Fools!

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.020
What'd you say?!

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:40.990
"You must abandon the many things
you've acquired as a human."

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:44.770
That is one of the conditions
to become a Phi-Brain.

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:46.030
Is it not?

00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:50.740
That which must be abandoned:

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:52.830
The past, emotions...

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:54.160
and...

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:56.280
friends.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:59.990
Everything is for the
completion of Phi-Brain.

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.770
That's what I thought, but...

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:05.680
Is killing really necessary?

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.180
The question was supposed
to come after you'd won.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:12.330
Oh, I'm just talking to myself.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:16.780
Sure enough, taking the shortest route

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:18.690
would have led to a dead end.

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:24.580
He proceeds without
hesitation, doesn't he?

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:25.990
That's Galileo, all right.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:31.740
Damn, what am I doing?

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.550
This ain't like me.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:38.510
Congratulations on winning
the puzzle championship,

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:40.680
Mr. Gammon Sakanoue.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.500
I'm most happy.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:48.360
To have a gifted student like you
attending Root Gakuen...

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:50.970
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:53.900
I solve prizes for the money.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:55.120
For me!

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.520
Perfectly acceptable.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:00.180
Your appearance when you challenge
puzzles with indomitable spirit,

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.590
when you arrive at the answer...

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:05.460
it invokes the image of a
certain illustrious man.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.820
Mr. Gammon Sakanoue...

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:11.380
I would like to bestow on
you the title of "Galileo."

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:17.540
I didn't used to care
about anythin' but money.

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:21.620
I ain't gonna get a single
dime from this puzzle.

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:24.420
It's his fault.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:28.090
I get pissed every time
he solves a puzzle.

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:30.590
This ain't like me at all!

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.620
<i>Galileo has cleared the third gate.</i>

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:40.030
Time and again, Kaito's friends have been

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:41.860
drawn into deadly puzzles.

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:45.910
There must be some other
intent at work, yes?

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:53.740
For example...

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.160
Yes!

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.210
Personal emotions, or something.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:03.460
That's check.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:08.720
Dammit! Where are you, Gammon?!

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:21.230
Damn, this city's like a puzzle!

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:26.850
What the?

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.240
This canal's shape...

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:40.900
This is the last area.

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:45.590
Th..This is...

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.600
Castling.

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:09.430
The rook protects its king...

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:10.710
Is that it?

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:18.100
This is purely conjecture-

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:19.330
Check.

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:26.570
Achieving the intellectual
pinnacle that is Phi-Brain

00:16:26.570 --> 00:16:28.780
would require a trial by
fire with one's comrades.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:29.780
Check.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.300
A double check?

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:41.250
<i>The rook that should be protecting its</i>

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.200
<i>
own army's king is after my king.</i>

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:47.010
<i>Even if he let my king go...</i>

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:49.190
It is unnecessary.

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:52.350
A "trial by fire with one's comrades,"

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:54.510
your Section Phi...

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:55.950
It's all unnecessary.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.750
What the hell's gonna happen?

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:15.470
There's no solution?!

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:18.100
Damn you, POG!

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:21.790
He's lost, lost!

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:32.000
What the?!

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.430
This thing could crash
just riding normally!

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:37.450
The water level's rising...

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.030
It can't be!

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:41.020
It's the high tide?

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:45.870
Gammon!

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:48.790
Dammit!

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:50.290
Gammon!

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:58.680
They made it through!

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:00.680
Kaito...

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:02.590
What the hell are you doing here?!

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:03.290
Huh?

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:04.220
Get outta here!

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.090
This puzzle is mine!

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:07.630
Why you...

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:08.940
Hurry and get off!

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:10.620
We're outta time!

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:11.870
Gimme that for a minute.

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:14.130
Bastard, what are you doing?!

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:15.280
This is...

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.150
Give it back.

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.390
Don't interfere!

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.820
This puzzle's got no answer!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.830
For them to go this far...

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:29.580
Rook!

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:32.840
Kaito...

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.520
Hey! Get off!

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:38.540
The water level...

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:40.470
The width of the canal...

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:41.890
Got it.

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:48.250
Hey, it's way too narrow to turn there!

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:59.040
The high tide changed the water level.

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:01.840
That opens up more room in the canal,
letting you turn!

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:05.330
The timing of the water rising...

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:07.160
The fact that this is the only place

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.050
where the puzzle could be solved...

00:19:09.050 --> 00:19:12.130
He saw all that in a second?

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:15.500
It's the fifth gate.

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:17.880
But we won't make it!

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.780
It can't be; he solved the
Labyrinth of Condemnation!

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:49.740
Kaito... He friggin' solved it!

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.740
That's it, Kaito.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.050
That's the spirit.

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:02.830
Kaito!

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:06.560
Are you all right, Kaito?

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.260
Hang in there!

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:12.310
Ana!

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:14.220
You still have some of my cookies?

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:15.020
Yes.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:15.960
Here!

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.540
Wake up, Kaito!

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:23.610
Kaito!

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.990
No!

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:32.530
Puzzle time is over!

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:35.060
We're going back to Japan!

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:38.680
A punch and Nonoha sweets?!

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:41.140
Any normal guy would've
died from that, 100%!

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:43.720
Kaito...

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:47.530
That woman!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:49.720
<i>Rook!</i>

00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:53.350
<i>I don't know what's up with you!</i>

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.110
<i>I don't know why you'd go this far!</i>

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.410
But I don't care about that.

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:01.600
If you want me, come get me, Rook.

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:04.340
We made a promise, didn't we?

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:07.500
I would solve all your puzzles!

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:11.930
An utter defeat, Mr. Director.

00:21:12.990 --> 00:21:16.040
I had a measure of confidence
in my chess skills,

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:17.950
but I've learned much.

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:19.940
Please play with me again.

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:21.250
If you'll excuse me.

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:35.730
My, my, I took on an
incredible adversary.

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.820
Huh? My juice?

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:44.240
No matter, I learned a lot.

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:47.700
Possessiveness and jealousy, eh?

00:21:48.520 --> 00:21:53.540
He hasn't yet abandoned all his humanity.

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:51.060
Am I catching a cold?

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:53.540
You cure a cold with green onions!

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:00.100
What a pitiful performance!

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:03.100
You bragged how you
would solve it yourself,

00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:05.560
but in the end, Kaito Daimon
saved you, didn't he?

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:06.470
Damn!

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:10.820
Be grateful that he kept
you from dying, Galileo.

00:22:10.820 --> 00:22:12.830
Rather, you lowly star.

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:16.800
He played me for a fool...

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.040
I'll make them all know!

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:21.770
The sun and the moon!

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:28.300
You bastards revolve around me!

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:05.390
Is it true that the school
principal went missing?

00:24:05.390 --> 00:24:06.860
It would seem so.

00:24:06.860 --> 00:24:09.490
He's not up to something again, is he?

00:24:09.490 --> 00:24:10.810
The principal?

00:24:10.810 --> 00:24:13.550
If that's so, I'm sure there's
nothing to worry about.

00:24:13.910 --> 00:24:14.950
Probably.

00:24:14.950 --> 00:24:16.740
The principal is with the POG.

00:24:16.740 --> 00:24:17.680
What?!

00:24:17.680 --> 00:24:20.350
They got to him, just like us!

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:22.910
Next time, "The Truth"

00:24:22.620 --> 00:24:27.550
The Truth

00:24:22.910 --> 00:24:26.110
You'll finally have your time
in the spotlight, Mr. Principal.
